From: Garrett Brown <eigendebugger@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix atomic initializer with Clang

Clang rejects a braced initializer for a C atomic scalar. Use the C17
initialization macro, which also supports the struct-based compatibility
implementations used by rcutils on older compilers and Windows.

diff --git a/src/testing/fault_injection.c b/src/testing/fault_injection.c
--- a/src/testing/fault_injection.c
+++ b/src/testing/fault_injection.c
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 
 #include "rcutils/stdatomic_helper.h"
 
-static atomic_int_least64_t g_rcutils_fault_injection_count = {-1};
+static atomic_int_least64_t g_rcutils_fault_injection_count = ATOMIC_VAR_INIT(-1);
 
 void rcutils_fault_injection_set_count(int_least64_t count)
 {
